{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqf906vsjhu","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"feature tier uses parallel git functions and a lightweight overlay feature record","summary":"For the stay-remote two-tier topology, the feature tier is implemented as PARALLEL functions in lib/git.js (createFeatureWorktree / mergeFeature / removeFeatureWorktree, branch prefix orch/feature/<slug>, worktree dir feature-<slug>) rather than generalizing createWorktree/mergeBranch in place — keeps the live attempt tier untouched and the diff small. The feature grouping node is a LIGHTWEIGHT overlay record (overlay.features[key] = {feature_branch, feature_worktree, base, createdAt}) via setFeature, not a new graph node kind — enough for the dashboard to show feature -> tasks. attempt->feature reuses existing primitives with zero new merge code: branch_task(base=orch/feature/<slug>, repo_path=<feature worktree>) forks the attempt off the feature branch, and merge_attempt(repo_path=<feature worktree>) runs mergeBranch in the feature worktree so the attempt lands on the FEATURE branch, never main. merge_feature is the only feature->main path and is dispatcher-gated tier-2: it appears in NO auto/heartbeat/loop/judge/decideAll path.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T13:27:48.952Z","vec":[-0.10047685354948044,-0.0020155597012490034,0.054207347333431244,0.048613060265779495,-0.002746428595855832,-0.0896645188331604,-0.06955261528491974,0.06663579493761063,-0.010449822060763836,-0.0031875118147581816,-0.00631492305546999,-0.038148388266563416,0.008783881552517414,-0.004519486799836159,0.10239693522453308,0.0032668060157448053,0.037691134959459305,0.040812183171510696,-0.004278103355318308,-0.08169267326593399,0.014742339961230755,-0.01588968187570572,-0.03129797801375389,0.059842437505722046,0.06260722130537033,-0.04724503681063652,-0.1191888377070427,-0.022471869364380836,0.013135782442986965,-0.0484938845038414,0.015228179283440113,0.04994364455342293,-0.0798997655510902